(1) Every victim has the right to obtain:
a. protection from individuals, groups and institutions both government and non-government;
b. access and information about the location of complaint centers, PPT, and all matters related to the fulfillment of rights and involvement in the decision-making process related to assistance and case development;
c. services that include medical, extensive medicolegal, psychosocial and legal;
d. handling that does not stop until physical and psychological recovery, but until the victim can resume life in society including the restoration of their good name;
e. confidential handling which includes guarantee of certainty for the victim that their identity will not be disseminated, medical care and legal handling;
f. assistance provided by psychologists to victims suffering from trauma/other mental problems to restore the victim's mental condition;
-9-
g. legal aid assistance provided by persons and/or legal aid institutions to victims at every level of examination and throughout the legal process; and
h. guarantee of rights related to the victim's status.
(2) Every child in conflict with the law has the right to obtain:
a. the right to have their identity kept confidential and not disclosed;
b. the right to obtain Legal Aid at every stage of examination, from investigation to the sentencing stage; and
c. the right to obtain an accompanying person at every stage of examination, from investigation to the sentencing stage.

REGENT OF NORTH BUTON,

Considering

a. that one of the objectives of the State to be achieved is to protect all Indonesian people and the entire Indonesian homeland so that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence;

b. that violence against women and children in North Buton Regency shows quite high numbers and continues to increase, so that protection efforts are needed;

c. that to provide a foundation and legal certainty for the protection of women and children victims of violence, it needs to be stipulated by Regional Regulation;

d. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to stipulate a Regional Regulation on the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of

1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235);

3. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

4. Law Number 13 of 2006 on Witness and Victim Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 64, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4635) as amended by Law Number 13 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 13 of 2006 on Witness and Victim Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 293, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4602);

5. Law Number 14 of 2007 concerning the Establishment of North Buton Regency in Southeast Sulawesi Province (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2007 Number 16, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4690);

6. Law Number 11 of 2012 concerning the Juvenile Criminal Justice System (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2012 Number 153, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5332);

7. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times, most recently by Law Number 11 of 2020 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2020 Number 245, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6573);

8. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning the Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

9. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Women's Protection;

10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 3 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Child Protection;

11. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 2036) as amended by Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 120 of 2018 concerning Amendment to Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 80 of 2015 concerning the Formation of Regional Legal Products (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2018 Number 157);

With the Mutual Approval of
THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES OF NORTH BUTON REGENCY
