a. provide services as quickly as possible and free of charge to Victims;
b. organize Protection and fulfillment of victims' rights to Medical Rehabilitation, Social Rehabilitation, Repatriation, social reintegration and legal assistance;
c. cooperate with certain institutions in providing translators and volunteer assistants needed for Victims;
d. network with government or private hospitals for treatment and health recovery of Victims and cooperate with witness and Victim Protection institutions, social Protection houses or trauma centers owned by the government, community, or other institutions for the health recovery of Victims;
e. provide convenience, comfort, and safety for Victims;
f. maintain the confidentiality of Victims;
g. provide economic empowerment;
-12-
h. provide fulfillment of legal assistance for Victims; and
1. in the event that integrated service delivery is carried out in a networked manner, PPT remains responsible for the entire referral process of services needed by Victims.
(2) The provision of integrated services as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in accordance with SPM.

Article 6
Neglect as referred to in Article 2 letter d is caused by:
a. acts that result in the failure to fulfill the needs of children properly, whether physical, mental, spiritual or social, committed by parents, guardians, or other parties responsible for care;
b. acts of deliberately neglecting to maintain, care for, or look after children as appropriate, committed by parents, guardians or any other party responsible for their care;
c. acts that neglect a person within the household scope, whereas according to the law applicable to them or due to agreement or contract, they are obligated to provide livelihood, care, or maintenance to that person; and/or
d. acts that result in economic dependence by means of restricting and/or prohibiting proper work inside or outside the home so that the victim is under the control of that person.

Article 15
SPM for Integrated Services for Women and Children, includes services: a. handling of complaints/reports of Women and Children Victims of Violence;
b. health services for Women and Children Victims of Violence; c. law enforcement and legal assistance for Women and Children Victims of Violence;
d. repatriation for Women and Children Victims of Violence; e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medicolegal for Women and Children Victims of Violence; and
f. psychological services for Women and Children Victims of Violence;

Article 10
(1) The Regional Government has the obligation and responsibility in providing Protection to Women and Children Victims of Violence.
